### UserController HTTP Client
### IntelliJ HTTP Client for testing UserController endpoints

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### Create User (POST /users)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Create User - Valid Email Format
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "user@domain.com",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

###

### Create User - Invalid Email Format (should return validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Create User - Short Password (should return validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "123"
}

###

### Create User - Missing Email (should return validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Create User - Missing Password (should return validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com"
}

###

### Create User - Duplicate Email (should return error if user already exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "duplicate@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Expected Response Format:
### Status: 201 Created
### Headers: Location: /users/{id}
### Body: {"id": {user_id}}